{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/932418-aliens-and-weird-fiction-in-cofd","id":932418,"title":"Aliens and weird fiction in CofD","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-07-15T23:18:53-07:00","id":932418,"title":"Aliens and weird fiction in CofD","content":"I was wondering how many of you enjoy throwing out all the occult stuff and using things like the men in black, aliens, the god machine, yeerks, reptilians, phychics, the thing, brain parasites, and cryptids in your games instead? I thought it might be fun to do a scifi horror chronicle that focuses on humans engaging mysteries and conspiracys instead of vampires and werewolves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12094,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12094-k9ine","user":"K9ine","date":". 07-16-2016, 02:28 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12094-k9ine","name":"K9ine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12094_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"270"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-16T02:31:40-07:00","id":932450,"title":"","content":"It's not really an either/or situation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-16T09:47:26-07:00","id":932543,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/932418-aliens-and-weird-fiction-in-cofd?p=932450#post932450\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's not really an either/or situation.</div> </div> </div> </div>My point is that it could be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12094-k9ine","name":"K9ine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12094_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"270"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-16T14:37:58-07:00","id":932636,"title":"","content":"Look at it this way; you could easily do a fairly standard Werewolf game that deals primarily with Claimed and one of the Idigam, and that's still a chronicle about psychic parasites and an alien immaterial monster from the Moon. It's all in the terms you couch things in. Hell, if you take a jump over to Night's Black Agents, the Dracula Dossier presents an alternative origin to Dracula in that he's reanimated by an interstellar bacterium that feeds on the telluric fields of the Earth and the strange gasses deep beneath the surface of Romania. <br /> <br /> It really doesn't take a lot of work to reskin traditional mythology into something weird and cosmic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-16T15:15:55-07:00","id":932649,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/932418-aliens-and-weird-fiction-in-cofd?p=932636#post932636\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Look at it this way; you could easily do a fairly standard Werewolf game that deals primarily with Claimed and one of the Idigam, and that's still a chronicle about psychic parasites and an alien immaterial monster from the Moon. It's all in the terms you couch things in. Hell, if you take a jump over to Night's Black Agents, the Dracula Dossier presents an alternative origin to Dracula in that he's reanimated by an interstellar bacterium that feeds on the telluric fields of the Earth and the strange gasses deep beneath the surface of Romania. <br /> <br /> It really doesn't take a lot of work to reskin traditional mythology into something weird and cosmic.</div> </div> </div> </div>OK.. but how would you feel if you were watching close encounters of the third kind and vampires showed up? I'm talking about NO occult.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12094-k9ine","name":"K9ine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12094_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"270"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-16T18:23:31-07:00","id":932716,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>K9ine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/932418-aliens-and-weird-fiction-in-cofd?p=932649#post932649\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">OK.. but how would you feel if you were watching close encounters of the third kind and vampires showed up? I'm talking about NO occult.</div> </div> </div> </div>If the vampire was an escaped lab experiment with needles for dingers, no mouth, and used the rules for Obfuscate but described as an implanted reflective field in its skin? Perfectly fine.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-16T22:26:03-07:00","id":932792,"title":"","content":"Happened all the time in X-files. Didn't seem to stop anybody there, either.<br /> <br /> Really, the &quot;mainstream&quot; UFO community believes in astral projection and can't even agree on whether the greys are from Zeta Reticuli (a phsyical impossibility, I might add), are faeries, are demons, or are humans from the post-singularity future projecting themselves back in time inside a computer simulation of reality. Half the community believes that bigfoots are dimensional interlopers with psychic invisibility fields and telekinesis. There are people who believe the Dulce base with all its aliens and mutants is also a clearing house for the demonic magic of the reptilians.<br /> <br /> Mekhet backstory involves a giant bug monster - could it be a mutant sea louse whose progeny are corpses controlled by the bugs in question? Could Nosferatu be animated by psychic parasites from the astral plane?<br /> <br /> What bout DMT and its links to spiritual beliefs in regards to dimensional entities in control of the flow of life and death? Could that be linked to Sin-Eaters and Geists?<br /> <br /> Could John C. Lilly's Solid State Intelligence and ECCO be linked to the God Machine?<br /> <br /> Are the greys a cryptid, a God-Machine plot, a spirit of fear of hospitals, fey abductors, manifestations of the divine fire shooting itself off without knowledge of what it's doing, searching endlessly for psychic context, or are they really humans from the post-singularity future?<br /> <br /> Are werewolves a segment of humanity that has learned to self-observe from several universes at once, and now at least one of those universes has noted - one from which they must feed to prevent themselves from experiencing quantum annihilation?<br /> <br /> If you're doping UFO culture and aliens into your WoD, you've already gone full occult.<br /> <br /> Speaking of, though, one of my STs ran a badass adventure series linking Resident Evil, the Thing, Starcraft, and the Mi-Go into one solid believable chunk.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4170-raygungoth","name":"raygungoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4170_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"144"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-16T23:26:34-07:00","id":932812,"title":"","content":"I have been mulling this over. While (at least in my approach) the line between sci fi horror and supernatural horror is fuzzy at best, I do feel your choice of theme and flavor has a tangible impact of player expectations and how they approach the problem solving.<br /> <br /> I would be interested in seeing the results of running a session with different groups but with a similar premise - A mysterious organization is abducting people and extracting their brain matter for a otherworldly patron. In one scenario, the patron is a Extraterrestrial, and the organization uses strange techno-organic devices. In the other, the patron is an eldritch entity and they use ancient ritual tools. In all other respects (locations, encounters, npcs) the scenarios are the same.<br /> <br /> Does the shift in genre trappings create a fundamentally different experience, or do the trappings not matter much overall?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1420009-the-artificer-s-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">The Artificer's Workshop</a> - A collection of Exalted Artifacts<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806809-curios-relics-and-tomes\" target=\"_blank\">Curios, Relics, and Tomes</a> - A collection of Relics (Cursed and Otherwise)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show\" target=\"_blank\">The Horror Lab</a> - A collection of Beasts, Monsters and less definable things.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1128197-strange-places#post1128197\" target=\"_blank\">Strange Places</a> - A collection of Dark, Mysterious, and Wondrous Locations<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie\" target=\"_blank\">Twilight Menagerie</a> - A collection of Ephemeral Entities","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","name":"Reighnhell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar775_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"749"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-17T01:02:32-07:00","id":932834,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reighnhell</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/932418-aliens-and-weird-fiction-in-cofd?p=932812#post932812\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does the shift in genre trappings create a fundamentally different experience, or do the trappings not matter much overall?</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem I have is that those two ideas are at their root very similiar. It's Lovecraft. The Eldritch Abominations are aliens. I think raygungoth has a really good point about the cross-over in both real life ufology and in fiction too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-17T11:59:15-07:00","id":932987,"title":"","content":"Lovecraft would make the space one Umbra, take advantage of the sea, the wastelands and perfectly combine the Sci-Fi for all of Aliens and any kind with the supernatural. Other than that I think is beyond the scope.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/641-ben-linus","name":"Ben Linus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-17T14:02:41-07:00","id":933041,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>raygungoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/932418-aliens-and-weird-fiction-in-cofd?p=932792#post932792\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Happened all the time in X-files. Didn't seem to stop anybody there, either.<br /> <br /> Really, the &quot;mainstream&quot; UFO community believes in astral projection and can't even agree on whether the greys are from Zeta Reticuli (a phsyical impossibility, I might add), are faeries, are demons, or are humans from the post-singularity future projecting themselves back in time inside a computer simulation of reality. Half the community believes that bigfoots are dimensional interlopers with psychic invisibility fields and telekinesis. There are people who believe the Dulce base with all its aliens and mutants is also a clearing house for the demonic magic of the reptilians.<br /> <br /> Mekhet backstory involves a giant bug monster - could it be a mutant sea louse whose progeny are corpses controlled by the bugs in question? Could Nosferatu be animated by psychic parasites from the astral plane?<br /> <br /> What bout DMT and its links to spiritual beliefs in regards to dimensional entities in control of the flow of life and death? Could that be linked to Sin-Eaters and Geists?<br /> <br /> Could John C. Lilly's Solid State Intelligence and ECCO be linked to the God Machine?<br /> <br /> Are the greys a cryptid, a God-Machine plot, a spirit of fear of hospitals, fey abductors, manifestations of the divine fire shooting itself off without knowledge of what it's doing, searching endlessly for psychic context, or are they really humans from the post-singularity future?<br /> <br /> Are werewolves a segment of humanity that has learned to self-observe from several universes at once, and now at least one of those universes has noted - one from which they must feed to prevent themselves from experiencing quantum annihilation?<br /> <br /> If you're doping UFO culture and aliens into your WoD, you've already gone full occult.<br /> <br /> Speaking of, though, one of my STs ran a badass adventure series linking Resident Evil, the Thing, Starcraft, and the Mi-Go into one solid believable chunk.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not interested in exploring how supernatural creatures interact with sci Fi elements in depth. If I was going to make a game with this stuff vampires would not exist. It would be an alternative wod world. I feel like it clashes with the weird fiction tone. vampires and werewolves evoke familiarity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12094-k9ine","name":"K9ine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12094_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"270"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-17T14:09:19-07:00","id":933044,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reighnhell</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/932418-aliens-and-weird-fiction-in-cofd?p=932812#post932812\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have been mulling this over. While (at least in my approach) the line between sci fi horror and supernatural horror is fuzzy at best, I do feel your choice of theme and flavor has a tangible impact of player expectations and how they approach the problem solving.<br /> <br /> I would be interested in seeing the results of running a session with different groups but with a similar premise - A mysterious organization is abducting people and extracting their brain matter for a otherworldly patron. In one scenario, the patron is a Extraterrestrial, and the organization uses strange techno-organic devices. In the other, the patron is an eldritch entity and they use ancient ritual tools. In all other respects (locations, encounters, npcs) the scenarios are the same.<br /> <br /> Does the shift in genre trappings create a fundamentally different experience, or do the trappings not matter much overall?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think when you go into horror people have one of two mind sets. One is where there is a spiritual truth, good/evil, possibility of the Divine. The other is ultimately nillistic, athistic, or gives no great importance to humanity. the physical and spiritual world's can exist in both versions, but they evoke different tones.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12094-k9ine","name":"K9ine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12094_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"270"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-17T15:56:42-07:00","id":933109,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>K9ine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/932418-aliens-and-weird-fiction-in-cofd?p=933041#post933041\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm not interested in exploring how supernatural creatures interact with sci Fi elements in depth. If I was going to make a game with this stuff vampires would not exist. It would be an alternative wod world. I feel like it clashes with the weird fiction tone. vampires and werewolves evoke familiarity.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, what elements are you planning on using?<br /> <br /> Maybe it would help if you were more specific - because &quot;weird fiction&quot; does encompass vampires and werewolves, just in a different context than &quot;magical dead guy.&quot; The process of weird fiction is very different from modern definitions of &quot;science fiction&quot; and &quot;fantasy&quot; in that it is from a period in which there was no division between the two. &quot;Occult&quot; merely means &quot;knowledge which is occluded,&quot; and pulps and weird fiction are rife with vampires and werewolves. What I was trying to explain is that the terminology isn't specific, and &quot;weird fiction&quot; encompasses far more of spec-fic than what you're talking about, so maybe provide some tropes here and there? Something to work with - because, otherwise, &quot;supernature&quot; has to encompass what is, in our world, not a component of nature - which includes nearly everything in section 000 and 130 in the public library.<br /> <br /> What I'm getting at is that these words - &quot;vampire&quot; and &quot;werewolf&quot; - much like &quot;demon&quot; - could be broadly applied to a wide spectrum of creatures, mythologies, technologies, and belief structures. These things aren't even &quot;real,&quot; physically, but they're real to communities and subcultures, so, when you're constructing a fictional context in which to place your potential stories, you have to decide how these physically incorrect assumptions interact with the reality of your fictional context (one of my professors called it &quot;mythic interfacing,&quot; which is such a cool term I had to bring it up). I am merely saying that the same groups of people who believe in aliens <i>also </i>tend to believe in vampires.<br /> <br /> So, how about instead of saying &quot;yeah but no supernatural or occult stuff,&quot; which is a statement that has very little meaning, considering that UFO lore is technically &quot;occult stuff,&quot; throw out some tropes. I see your example media list, and <a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/ArbitrarySkepticism\" target=\"_blank\">none of those things preclude the existence of werewolves</a>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4170,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4170-raygungoth","user":"raygungoth","date":". 07-17-2016, 06:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4170-raygungoth","name":"raygungoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4170_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"144"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-17T19:30:04-07:00","id":933205,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>raygungoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/932418-aliens-and-weird-fiction-in-cofd?p=933109#post933109\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, what elements are you planning on using?<br /> <br /> Maybe it would help if you were more specific - because &quot;weird fiction&quot; does encompass vampires and werewolves, just in a different context than &quot;magical dead guy.&quot; The process of weird fiction is very different from modern definitions of &quot;science fiction&quot; and &quot;fantasy&quot; in that it is from a period in which there was no division between the two. &quot;Occult&quot; merely means &quot;knowledge which is occluded,&quot; and pulps and weird fiction are rife with vampires and werewolves. What I was trying to explain is that the terminology isn't specific, and &quot;weird fiction&quot; encompasses far more of spec-fic than what you're talking about, so maybe provide some tropes here and there? Something to work with - because, otherwise, &quot;supernature&quot; has to encompass what is, in our world, not a component of nature - which includes nearly everything in section 000 and 130 in the public library.<br /> <br /> What I'm getting at is that these words - &quot;vampire&quot; and &quot;werewolf&quot; - much like &quot;demon&quot; - could be broadly applied to a wide spectrum of creatures, mythologies, technologies, and belief structures. These things aren't even &quot;real,&quot; physically, but they're real to communities and subcultures, so, when you're constructing a fictional context in which to place your potential stories, you have to decide how these physically incorrect assumptions interact with the reality of your fictional context (one of my professors called it &quot;mythic interfacing,&quot; which is such a cool term I had to bring it up). I am merely saying that the same groups of people who believe in aliens <i>also </i>tend to believe in vampires.<br /> <br /> So, how about instead of saying &quot;yeah but no supernatural or occult stuff,&quot; which is a statement that has very little meaning, considering that UFO lore is technically &quot;occult stuff,&quot; throw out some tropes. I see your example media list, and <a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/ArbitrarySkepticism\" target=\"_blank\">none of those things preclude the existence of werewolves</a>.</div> </div> </div> </div>I gave examples in the first post. Modern myths, things that you see more in the 80's and onward, from the Men in Black to Slenderman. I thought I made it clear but I guess not many people understood what I was talking about. Another example would be anything that was in the public conciousness once technology and skeptism rose up over religion and more rural ways of life.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12094-k9ine","name":"K9ine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12094_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"270"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-17T22:53:56-07:00","id":933275,"title":"","content":"Men in black mythology dates back to the 1940s. Slenderman mythology retroactively includes German and Russian mythology and is very heavily tied into occult circles - I know people who think the damn thing is real and its appearance on the internet was caused by psychic backlash of said entity trying to create itself backwards through the past.<br /> <br /> Modern mythology makes heavy use of the astral plane, vampirism, witchcraft, werewolves, and <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/John_C._Lilly#Solid_State_Intelligence\" target=\"_blank\">god-machine like entities</a>. If you're going to bring in the MKULTRA experiments, DMT, the New Age movement, and so on, those things are already there - in spades.<br /> <br /> You <i>do</i> know reptilian alien mythology also incorporates goddamn SATAN, alternate psychic dimensions, vampires, and basically the entire content of Mage: the Awakening, right?<br /> <br /> You are aware that the modern New Age shamanism movements that include alien greys and blues and nordics <i>also</i> includes m-shifting and p-shifting components of werewolf mythology, right?<br /> <br /> You know that Demon: the Descent and Changeling: the Lost are essentially Modern UFO Lore: the RPG with almost zero fiddling required, right?<br /> <br /> I'm trying to ask where the damn line is, for crying out loud. - Be more specific than just a few examples. What's in, what's out? What is it <i>about</i> vampires that puts them outside your ideas (I can stat The Thing as a Gangrel with just about 10xp)? What is it <i>about</i> Mage: the Awakening that differentiates it from a psychic out of modern mythology (I'll give you a hint: <a href=\"http://www.crystalinks.com/psychic.html\" target=\"_blank\">almost nothing</a>)? You can't honestly tell me you can reconcile yeerks but not animal-based shapeshifters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4170-raygungoth","name":"raygungoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4170_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"144"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-18T00:29:23-07:00","id":933298,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>raygungoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/932418-aliens-and-weird-fiction-in-cofd?p=933275#post933275\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Men in black mythology dates back to the 1940s. Slenderman mythology retroactively includes German and Russian mythology and is very heavily tied into occult circles - I know people who think the damn thing is real and its appearance on the internet was caused by psychic backlash of said entity trying to create itself backwards through the past.<br /> <br /> Modern mythology makes heavy use of the astral plane, vampirism, witchcraft, werewolves, and <a href=\"http://&quot;&#91;url\" target=\"_blank\">https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/John_C._Lilly#Solid_State_Intelligence&quot;]god-machine</a> like entities[/URL]. If you're going to bring in the MKULTRA experiments, DMT, the New Age movement, and so on, those things are already there - in spades.<br /> <br /> You <i>do</i> know reptilian alien mythology also incorporates goddamn SATAN, alternate psychic dimensions, vampires, and basically the entire content of Mage: the Awakening, right?<br /> <br /> You are aware that the modern New Age shamanism movements that include alien greys and blues and nordics <i>also</i> includes m-shifting and p-shifting components of werewolf mythology, right?<br /> <br /> You know that Demon: the Descent and Changeling: the Lost are essentially Modern UFO Lore: the RPG with almost zero fiddling required, right?<br /> <br /> I'm trying to ask where the damn line is, for crying out loud. - Be more specific than just a few examples. What's in, what's out? What is it <i>about</i> vampires that puts them outside your ideas (I can stat The Thing as a Gangrel with just about 10xp)? What is it <i>about</i> Mage: the Awakening that differentiates it from a psychic out of modern mythology (I'll give you a hint: <a href=\"http://&quot;&#91;url\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.crystalinks.com/psychic.html&quot;]almost</a> nothing[/URL])? You can't honestly tell me you can reconcile yeerks but not animal-based shapeshifters.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't want the high fantasy/Gothic/romanticised style of those splats. As soon as some one hears the name of a old world mythological creature, the modern myth is consumed by it. Yes I knew all that stuff, but the trappings and names need to be taken away. vampires might become face morphing parasites that eat brain matter instead of sucking blood. Changelings lose all the bestial/tree/elf aspects and become cyborgs or augmented psychics. Do you understand?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12094,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12094-k9ine","user":"K9ine","date":". 07-18-2016, 03:31 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12094-k9ine","name":"K9ine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12094_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"270"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-18T00:54:54-07:00","id":933309,"title":"","content":"Okay, I think I get what you're saying now. Alright. This can be worked with. Honestly, the Chronicles of Darkness has done away with a lot of the gothic/romanticised aspects of the old setting and has made things a lot more personal and localized - as well as blurred the lines between what is high fantasy and what isn't (which a lot of modern occult mythology has already done for us - Men in black mythology, for example, is often conflated and identical to with older stories about directly confronting devils).<br /> <br /> I have run a &quot;Demon&quot; game in which the PCs were turned into quantum self-observers due to an accident regarding their work on a particle accelerator. Another of my STs runs a hard-SF space travel campaign where our problems tend to be stuff like &quot;oh no, we're out of neodymium and therefore going to die because we can't repair our fusion generators during cycle down periods!&quot;<br /> <br /> I think the trappings behind the names can only be taken away if you apply the name and then challenge the assumptions behind it. If your players hear &quot;vampire&quot; and start planning to deal with gothic undead bloodsuckers, they are totally unprepared for fear-based psychic parasites that reproduce by scaring people to death, or for alien bug-monsters that camouflage themselves asthe palate and lower sinuses whose mandibles stick out where you'd expect to see fangs.<br /> <br /> I submit that allowing a player's assumptions to inform them as to what they think they know might be a valid technique for introducing those concepts - that's what I was getting at earlier with those questions about linking DMT visions to Geists and UFO mythology to Demon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4170-raygungoth","name":"raygungoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4170_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"144"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-18T14:02:40-07:00","id":933576,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>raygungoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/932418-aliens-and-weird-fiction-in-cofd?p=933309#post933309\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, I think I get what you're saying now. Alright. This can be worked with. Honestly, the Chronicles of Darkness has done away with a lot of the gothic/romanticised aspects of the old setting and has made things a lot more personal and localized - as well as blurred the lines between what is high fantasy and what isn't (which a lot of modern occult mythology has already done for us - Men in black mythology, for example, is often conflated and identical to with older stories about directly confronting devils).<br /> <br /> I have run a &amp;quot;Demon&amp;quot; game in which the PCs were turned into quantum self-observers due to an accident regarding their work on a particle accelerator. Another of my STs runs a hard-SF space travel campaign where our problems tend to be stuff like &amp;quot;oh no, we're out of neodymium and therefore going to die because we can't repair our fusion generators during cycle down periods!&amp;quot;<br /> <br /> I think the trappings behind the names can only be taken away if you apply the name and then challenge the assumptions behind it. If your players hear &amp;quot;vampire&amp;quot; and start planning to deal with gothic undead bloodsuckers, they are totally unprepared for fear-based psychic parasites that reproduce by scaring people to death, or for alien bug-monsters that camouflage themselves asthe palate and lower sinuses whose mandibles stick out where you'd expect to see fangs.<br /> <br /> I submit that allowing a player's assumptions to inform them as to what they think they know might be a valid technique for introducing those concepts - that's what I was getting at earlier with those questions about linking DMT visions to Geists and UFO mythology to Demon.</div> </div> </div> </div>In a game like this I would never use the word vampire, even if I used a vampire discipline for it. I feel like even making them think in terms of familiar creatures sort of kills the mood id be going for.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12094-k9ine","name":"K9ine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12094_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"270"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-18T15:23:30-07:00","id":933607,"title":"","content":"Ironic you want to take the fantasy out of wod but your signature is from a fantasy character.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My name is Colleen. My favorite song is &quot;Wildwood Flower.&quot; My ambition is to write the complete history of the White Wolf/Onyx Path universe.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11905-julianmoon","name":"JulianMoon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"253"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-18T20:59:24-07:00","id":933728,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JulianMoon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/932418-aliens-and-weird-fiction-in-cofd?p=933607#post933607\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ironic you want to take the fantasy out of wod but your signature is from a fantasy character.</div> </div> </div> </div>I love fantasy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12094-k9ine","name":"K9ine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12094_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"270"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-18T23:36:25-07:00","id":933759,"title":"","content":"I'm honestly not sure what you're asking or what you object to in Chronicles of Darkness. ChroD has a ton of scifi horror elements. Are you saying you play ChroD using only Demons, Prometheans, aliens, and other weird science stuff? That could be interesting. How &quot;scientific&quot; do you want your horror? Aliens being little grey men who want to kidnap us and poke us for no good reason and people being able to blow stuff up with their minds are scifi, but they're still somewhat fantastical in nature. To give some examples, Star Wars is scifi-fantasy, The Martian is pure hard scifi, Alien is scifi-horror, and Warhammer 40k is scifi-horror-fantasy. Which of those are you going for?<br /> <br /> If you want a cosmic horror game that goes for pure science fiction without fantasy, try Eclipse Phase. It's spooky, it's fairly hard as scifi goes, and it's fantastic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-19T10:31:24-07:00","id":933966,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/932418-aliens-and-weird-fiction-in-cofd?p=933759#post933759\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm honestly not sure what you're asking or what you object to in Chronicles of Darkness. ChroD has a ton of scifi horror elements. Are you saying you play ChroD using only Demons, Prometheans, aliens, and other weird science stuff? That could be interesting. How &amp;quot;scientific&amp;quot; do you want your horror? Aliens being little grey men who want to kidnap us and poke us for no good reason and people being able to blow stuff up with their minds are scifi, but they're still somewhat fantastical in nature. To give some examples, Star Wars is scifi-fantasy, The Martian is pure hard scifi, Alien is scifi-horror, and Warhammer 40k is scifi-horror-fantasy. Which of those are you going for?<br /> <br /> If you want a cosmic horror game that goes for pure science fiction without fantasy, try Eclipse Phase. It's spooky, it's fairly hard as scifi goes, and it's fantastic.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like CofD as is, but I thought it might be fun to take out the familiar stuff. Sci-fi is probably best soft in horror, there should be things that can't be explained with science. The main thing is to make it feel new by removing the familiarity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12094-k9ine","name":"K9ine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12094_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"270"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-19T11:00:23-07:00","id":933979,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>K9ine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/932418-aliens-and-weird-fiction-in-cofd?p=933966#post933966\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I like CofD as is, but I thought it might be fun to take out the familiar stuff. Sci-fi is probably best soft in horror, there should be things that can't be explained with science. The main thing is to make it feel new by removing the familiarity.</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem with that is that it takes a lot of work to remove the &quot;familiar&quot; elements of Chronicles of Darkness, because it's deliberately designed to be &quot;familiar&quot; to some degree. Most of the supernatural characters and phenomena draw to some degree on recognizable archetypes. <br /> <br /> I'd suggest you check out The Book of Unremitting Horror. It's a collection of horror monsters for the GUMSHOE system, and they're designed to mostly all be new and unrecognizable and not based on existing monster types.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-19T11:15:57-07:00","id":933986,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/932418-aliens-and-weird-fiction-in-cofd?p=933979#post933979\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The problem with that is that it takes a lot of work to remove the &quot;familiar&quot; elements of Chronicles of Darkness, because it's deliberately designed to be &quot;familiar&quot; to some degree. Most of the supernatural characters and phenomena draw to some degree on recognizable archetypes.<br /> <br /> I'd suggest you check out The Book of Unremitting Horror. It's a collection of horror monsters for the GUMSHOE system, and they're designed to mostly all be new and unrecognizable and not based on existing monster types.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks, might check it out. Really though, I don't think its that hard if you use the horror creation system and pull things from the splat books while changing them slightly. I'm not trying to take away all similarities. Vampires might become brain suckers with tenticals that come out of their heads for instance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12094-k9ine","name":"K9ine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12094_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"270"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}